Trapping Rain Water - Problem Statement
You are given an array height[] of size n where each element represents the height of a building (or bar) of width 1.
After raining, water gets trapped between the buildings. Your task is to determine the total amount of water that can be trapped.

In cpp:
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    int arr[] = {4, 0, 2, 0, 1};

    int left = 0, right = 0;
    int c = 0;

    int n = sizeof(arr) / sizeof(arr[0]) - 1; // last index

    if (arr[0] > arr[n]) {
        left++;
    } else {
        right++;
    }

    if (left > 0) {
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            c += arr[n] - arr[i];
        }
    } else {
        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
            c += arr[0] - arr[i];
        }
    }

    cout << c;

    return 0;
}


